 operates proprietary and third-party cardlock, and sells fuel using proprietary fuel cards. The GPMP segment is involved in the wholesale distribution of fuel to the retail and wholesale segments. The company is based in Richmond, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Arie  Kotler | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 51 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $784K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $7K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["ARKO Corp. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $445M market cap on $7.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $65M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 8.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 30% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 64% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ARKO Corp (ARKO) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Raised EBITDA Guidance and 12th Straight ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo