en lumpy (year-to-year swings of 14%).","At current returns, reinvesting 1% of profits supports about 0.1% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 1.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 54.1% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 29.8%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 71%.","It returns 9.3% a year to shareholders (6.3% in buybacks and 3.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It pays out 240% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk.","Short interest is elevated at 10.9% of the float, 10.1 days to cover."],"people":["With about 9,748 employees, each generates about $784K of revenue, 2.1x the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $7K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.5M (3x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":52,"head":"Avoid: operating income covers interest only 1.1x.","pros":["Trades 64% below fair value of $11.10","P/FCF 6.8x vs sector 16.5x","2 analysts' mean target $8.50 (+114%)","Returns 9.3% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Revenue shrank 5.8%/yr over 3y","Interest coverage only 1.1x","P/E 79.4x vs sector 19.3x"],"flags":["Operating income covers interest only 1.1x"],"need":[],"buy_below":9.44,"vc":{"base":11.1,"base_src":"dcf","bear":8.18,"bull":15.24,"alt_median":3.4,"n_alt":3,"gap":3.758,"dispersion":0.333,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (33% dispersion)","DCF is 376% above the other models' median ($3.40)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"ARKO","date":"2026-11-06"}